From 516a47b4163f1fe03cd8d9af1b88b1d0051a1559 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 22:23:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] lifecycle guard: a script fed on a moved, chained or
 `exec`-opened descriptor is scanned (`bash 3<r.sh <&3-`, `exec 3<r.sh; bash
 <&3`)

PR #2702 made `bash 3<r.sh <&3` block: `<&N` after `N<f` in the same
command reads f. Sibling forms still fed r.sh to bash unscanned, and
scan_gateway_lifecycle returned (False, None) for a script that restarts
the gateway:

- Move form `bash 3<r.sh <&3-` / `0<&3-`: the target `3-` was looked up
  as-is and is never a key.
- `bash 3<r.sh 0>&3`: `0>&3` is dup2(3, 0) like `0<&3`.
- Chains: `bash 3<r.sh 4<&3 <&4`, `4<&3- <&4`.
- A descriptor opened by an earlier `exec` with only redirections, which
  keeps it open in the shell for later commands on the same line or later
  lines: `exec 3<r.sh; bash <&3`, `exec 3<r.sh && bash <&3`,
  `exec 3<r.sh; cat <&3 | bash`, `exec 3<r.sh; { bash; } <&3`,
  `exec 3<r.py; python3 <&3`, `exec <r.sh; bash <&0`.
- A redirection in command position (`3<r.sh bash <&3`,
  `3<r.sh cat <&3 | bash`, `exec 3<r.sh bash <&3`): the hoist moved it to
  the end, after the `<&3` that reads it.

Fix:
- New cron/lifecycle_guard_fds.py (lifecycle_guard.py sits at its
  FILE_LINES cap) holds REDIRECTION and split_redirections, now driven by
  one descriptor table (apply_redirection): `<`/`<>` open, `<&N`, `<&N-`
  and `0>&N` copy (a move also closes N), anything else clears.
- carry_exec_descriptors keeps the table across the lines of one command
  (`_iter_segment_contexts`): a redirection-only `exec` updates it (read
  wherever it stands, in a subshell or branch too: fail closed, the file
  is only scanned), and a later `<&N` the command did not set itself is
  rewritten to `< f`. Fast path when nothing is open and no `exec` token.
- _command_segment_views adds an in-order hoist (command-position
  redirections right after the command word, ahead of the command's own)
  before the existing end-hoist, which positional readers (`source x`,
  `launchctl submit`) still use.

Still allowed: `bash <&3 3<r.sh` (not open yet), `bash <&3; exec 3<r.sh`
(opened later), a clean script, the command's own `3<clean.sh` over a carried
`3<r.sh`, a carried descriptor closed (`exec 3<&-`), re-pointed or moved
away, `exec 3<r.sh true; bash <&3`, `bash 3<r.sh >&3`.

RED/GREEN: tests/cron/test_lifecycle_guard_descriptor_carry.py: 32 failed /
17 passed with cron/ at the #2702 head be63ac710f, 49 passed at head.
tests/cron + the five lifecycle-guard suites outside it via
run_tests.sh: 244 files, 3424 passed, 0 failed, 9 skipped. The 8000-line
heredoc timing test stays at base speed (~2.1 s vs ~2.0 s standalone).

Card: t_78b1ff930ed8af7c (found reviewing PR #2702, review 5898640962).
